<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William Mackinnon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1823">1823</a>–<a href="/years/1893">1893</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William Mackinnon was a Scottish shipping <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnates">magnate</a>, founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-india">British India</a> Steam Navigation Company. He founded the Imperial British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-africa">East Africa</a> Company, which received a royal charter in 1888 to administer the British sphere in East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, and backed the expedition to relieve Emin Pasha.</p></div>
